The '''Torre del Comerciant''' ({{lang|ca|Torre del Comerciant}}; "Merchant Tower") is a 48-storey office tower at 60 Carretera de Pedro González in the [[El Centre (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|El Centre]] barri of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. Completed in 2002, the tower was developed by [[BdSC Corporació]], the parent company of the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]], and stands one block from the stock exchange building. At 222 metres (728 ft), it is one of the tallest buildings in Sant Cristòfor.

== Architecture ==

The Torre del Comerciant is a slender modern corporate tower with a rectangular floor plate and a blue-green glass curtain wall. Strong vertical mullions emphasise its height, while a dark horizontal band around the middle of the shaft marks a mechanical or transfer level. Near the top, the façade steps inward slightly before reaching a steep, metallic pyramidal crown. A thin central spire gives the tower a distinctive skyline profile.

The base is formed by a broad, light-stone and glass podium containing the lobby, retail space, conference facilities, and parking access. The tower's formal, symmetrical composition and restrained detailing reflect the prestige office architecture of the late 1990s and early 2000s.

