== History ==

The Torre del Comerciant was constructed between 1999 and 2002 by [[BdSC Corporació]] as part of the modernisation of the financial district around the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]]. The tower was intended to provide premium office space for financial services firms, brokerages, law offices, and other institutions associated with the exchange. Its location one block from the Bolsa made it a natural extension of the city's financial services corridor.

The building's name references the commercial and merchant history of El Centre, where trading houses, banks, and insurance firms have been concentrated since the early 20th century.

== Use ==

The tower serves as an office building for financial and professional services tenants. The lower floors contain retail and conference facilities, while the upper floors are divided among corporate offices, investment managers, and legal and accounting firms tied to the nearby stock exchange.

